# K03 NS-ROLES-1b (Codex K03-NS-ROLES-NEXT-20261007-09; v3 M2; docs/LMX_semantics.en.md:304, :307, :398): after
# `box: Model` the held reference box selects Model, and `call: box` executes Model's body as `call: Model` does;
# bare `box` only reads the reference and `box()` is a structural form, not a call; nothing runs at the binding.
# At the root.  Exit 7; 81 otherwise.
int: hits 0
Model:
    int: v 1
    node\hits: node\hits + 1
end: Model
box: Model
call: box
fn: m () int
    if: node\hits != 1
        return: 81
    return: 7
end: m
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
